{"title":"Arbitration Associate Roadmap","role":"Arbitration Associate","summary":"An Arbitration Associate supports lawyers, arbitrators, companies, and clients in resolving commercial and other disputes through arbitration and alternative dispute resolution (ADR) rather than conventional court litigation.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Alternative Dispute Resolution / Arbitration & Mediation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Arbitration Associate supports lawyers, arbitrators, companies, and clients in resolving commercial and other disputes through arbitration and alternative dispute resolution (ADR) rather than conventional court litigation."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law","Contract Law","Dispute Resolution","Legal Research","Evidence","Procedure","Advocacy"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Arbitration Associates typically assist with case strategy, legal research, pleadings, evidence, procedural applications, hearings, arbitral awards, settlement negotiations, and enforcement proceedings."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Arbitration Associate is a legal practice role rather than a separate regulated degree. An LLB provides the academic foundation; independent practice as an advocate in India requires meeting applicable professional and Bar Council requirements. Specialist arbitration credentials can strengthen the profile but do not substitute for required legal qualifications where legal practice is involved."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Typical Work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Commercial Arbitration"},{"text":"Business and contractual disputes"}],[{"text":"Construction Arbitration"},{"text":"Infrastructure and construction claims"}],[{"text":"International A